#===============================================================================
# UNOS Liver Transplant Anti-Rejection Therapy Analysis
#
# Parses UNOS liver transplant patients into rejection-therapy groups
# (no rejection / steroid monotherapy / combined therapy / dual therapy) over
# the first year post-transplant, builds baseline demographic tables,
# propensity-score-matches treatment arms, and runs landmark + time-varying
# survival and year-2 outcome analyses.
#
# CLEANED VERSION -- reorganized into labeled sections and de-duplicated.
# No analysis logic was changed from the reviewed/patched version; changes
# here are purely structural:
#   - package loading collapsed into one loop
#   - the old hand-built gt() Table 1-5 blocks (which computed their own
#     summary stats and p-values from scratch) were removed, since the
#     gtsummary-based Table 1-5 block later in the script was already written
#     to reproduce the same five comparisons from the same cohort data frames
#     and was explicitly intended to replace them
#   - the now-dead helper functions that only fed those old tables
#     (calc_demo_stats, calc_demo_std, build_mean_vector, build_std_vector,
#     calc_pvalues, fmt_count, is_median_row, and the demo_label1/ref_value1/
#     header_rows label vectors) were removed along with them
#   - the gtsummary Table 1-5 block was moved up to where the old tables used
#     to live, right after the propensity-matched cohorts it depends on exist
#   - the donor-ID duplicate check was moved next to the deceased-donor
#     processing step it is diagnosing
#   - inline "[FIX n]" review-point tags were converted to plain explanatory
#     comments describing *why* the code does what it does, since the
#     numbering was only meaningful in the context of the original review
#===============================================================================


#===============================================================================
# 0. Libraries
#===============================================================================
