# NOTES / things to check before trusting this output:
# 1. Categorical p-values now come from gts_safe_cat_test(), which calls
#    safe_chisq_or_fisher() directly -- so the tables and the year-2 analyses
#    apply an identical chi-square/Fisher rule.
# 2. All continuous rows use a t-test. If MELD or cold ischemic time are
#    skewed and Wilcoxon is preferred instead, set that variable's test
#    individually, e.g. add_p(test = list(MELD_PELD_LAB_SCORE ~ "wilcox.test", ...)).
# 3. gtsummary always prints whatever footnote text is supplied in
#    modify_footnote() -- if a Wilcoxon test is added anywhere, update the
#    footnote string to say so.
# 4. HLA_MM, ORGAN_LBL, RACE_LBL, PREV_ANY_LBL are multi-level categorical
#    variables -> gtsummary prints one p-value on the variable's header row.
# 5. To export as Word/PDF, pipe into as_flex_table() (Word), as_gt() (further
#    gt customization), or as_kable_extra() (PDF via LaTeX).


